{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 72, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 72, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=73&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=71&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 521027230, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r521027230-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Religious", "text": "A great time in visiting this sacred place\nLots of arts crafted everywhere\nIdols and statues \nBe aware of monkeys around, they won't attack you but might steal your sweets ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2017-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "927576A7C14CF251C2409062DF067781", "name": "TheTravelling Boy", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/kandelbabs", "username": "kandelbabs", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f3/23/default-avatar-2020-28.jpg", "contribution_count": 171, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255100, "location_name": "Melbourne", "location_name_detailed": "Melbourne, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-09-04", "published_at_date": "2017-09-04"}, {"review_id": 521011956, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r521011956-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Great place for those who are interested in traditions", "text": "You can see traditions of burning dead people. We hired a guide there and he told us that you can pay whatever you want at the end. The enterence ticket was 1000 ruppies for each person and each of us paid 1000 ruppies for guide. I think guidance was helpfull for us since we where not familiar with hindus traditions.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "2BEA341720A287B422C867CAB2BA95AA", "name": "Hooshmand H", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/hooshmandh", "username": "hooshmandh", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0d/14/38/d2/hooshmand-h.jpg", "contribution_count": 11, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293999, "location_name": "Tehran", "location_name_detailed": "Tehran, Iran"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-09-04", "published_at_date": "2017-09-04"}, {"review_id": 520409039, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r520409039-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Very humbling", "text": "We witnessed 2 funerals taking place the day we came.  It was humbling to witness another culture/religion and their grieving. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4238C1274A58FD6FC70470A6115A019D", "name": "michellemN837RO", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/michellemN837RO", "username": "michellemN837RO", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e8/ea/default-avatar-2020-63.jpg", "contribution_count": 9, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-09-02", "published_at_date": "2017-09-02"}, {"review_id": 520309168, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r520309168-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Eco-adventurer", "text": "                                                Pashupatinath\n     Pashupatinath is very much a revered site, sacred to both Buddhists and Hindus. It is also a cremation grounds where cultural gatherings transpire...which includes regular ritual bathing.\nThis spot too is the home of nomadic yogis,many of which favor these grounds for the meditative atmosphere evoked by this pilgrimage locale.\n      One can request the renunciants to pose for photos..and often they are keen to demonstrate  \nHatha yoga postures known as asanas.\n      One time I was taken aback by a small group of snake charmers who were playing diverse hypnotic tunes on their folk instruments, much to the delight of all assembled. The gyrating spectacle sent a distinct chill up my spine as several of the six foot long cobras slithered in my\ndirection! Hence I beat a hasty retreat with my camera and tripod. I was prepared to keep the tripod legs fully extended to ward off the creatures who for some unknown reason seemed to share a growing fondness for my presence there. My retreat was successful...and I did not look back!  On he a subsequent visit I asked some local man about the charmer entourage. He\nmentioned  that this group was eventually banned from the site, most likely for safety reasons. \nYet today the wandering sadhus, decked out in their exotic finery, placid cows, and lively monkeys all seem to adore Pashupatinath.\n      As an aside, proper etiquette is to be sensitive about taking photos of the cremations taking place. Instead you might consider purchasing some local arts and crafts accoutrements such as miniature prayer wheels,Rudraksha neclklaces made from seeds,..and the like.  Whatever transpires, enjoy that which is both rare and beautiful.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2016-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "AFF5EAAEFB98BA56503344FED0796B58", "name": "Lorenanda", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Lorenanda", "username": "Lorenanda", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e2/a7/default-avatar-2020-44.jpg", "contribution_count": 44, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-09-01", "published_at_date": "2017-09-02"}, {"review_id": 519927689, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r519927689-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "History and spiritualism overshadowed", "text": "The manner in which the temple is managed is pathetic. the Pandits are rude and despite standing in serpant ques, you may end up not getting a dekko of Deity", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "business", "stay_date": "2017-07-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "3C65CCC43A97B29BCAE7AD3CA937D41C", "name": "nirav24", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/nirav24", "username": "nirav24", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/15/aa/96/d0/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 96, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304551, "location_name": "New Delhi", "location_name_detailed": "New Delhi, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-08-31", "published_at_date": "2017-09-01"}, {"review_id": 519651018, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r519651018-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Must-do in Kathmandu", "text": "One of the oldest temples in Nepal, Pashupatinath temple has a unique grandeur attached to it. Go around the aarti time to witness the whole experience.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "D8E740FE05602496333E45C449BEE4B6", "name": "Ritika J", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/782ritikaj", "username": "782ritikaj", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/58/79/44/ritika181.jpg", "contribution_count": 58, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 295424, "location_name": "Dubai", "location_name_detailed": "Dubai, United Arab Emirates"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-08-30", "published_at_date": "2017-08-31"}, {"review_id": 518643794, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r518643794-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Om namah Shivay", "text": "I have been to this temple twice and it was a very good experience to be there, we went in the afternoon time when it was sunny and our feet were burning with heat, morning is the best time to visit actually, but afternoon the rush is less hence we had finished with our pooja immidiately. The place requires lot of maintainance as there is cow dung spread every where.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2017-05-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "7B28D26F055F259D66EB86A95C5E4FBC", "name": "Anusha S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/560anushas", "username": "560anushas", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0f/b0/01/a8/sharmakanusha.jpg", "contribution_count": 52, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304554, "location_name": "Mumbai", "location_name_detailed": "Mumbai, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-08-29", "published_at_date": "2017-08-29"}, {"review_id": 518209764, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r518209764-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "the crematoria", "text": "it was very scary to see burning body but it was very different experience for us. the surrounding area and view of temple are excellent. the only disappointment was it was not allowed to non hindu so we could not go inside.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "7D19ED401644425B3F124D1FE79AF85E", "name": "khaliod m", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/khaliodm", "username": "khaliodm", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ea/b2/default-avatar-2020-69.jpg", "contribution_count": 8, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-08-28", "published_at_date": "2017-08-28"}, {"review_id": 517870891, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r517870891-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A bit In your face", "text": "It is an interesting temple to visit but it is a bit in your face with corpse burning on the riverside. It is dirty and muddy (as expected during the monsoon) but saw a couple of thefts and be aware of people trying to scam money of you. It is quite expensive to get in for foreigners 10 US $ per person and almost impossible to let to walk around alone so be prepared to pay for a guide. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2017-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "2649ABB80112145693CCE66322CCF8EA", "name": "acdenmark", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/acdenmark", "username": "acdenmark", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/08/d5/0d/10/acdenmark.jpg", "contribution_count": 717, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 294217, "location_name": "Hong Kong", "location_name_detailed": "Hong Kong, China"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/70/94/e3/photo0jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/70/94/e4/photo1jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/70/94/e5/photo2jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/70/94/e6/photo3jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/70/94/e7/photo4jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/70/94/e8/photo5jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/70/94/e9/photo6jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/70/94/ea/photo7jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/70/94/eb/photo8jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/70/94/ec/photo9jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-08-27", "published_at_date": "2017-08-27"}, {"review_id": 517776126, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g29